{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14267 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine is linked to Histone H1.0 through a series of molecular pathways that involve M-phase phosphoprotein 8, a target of multiple benzocaine derivatives. These derivatives, including (2S,3S)-2,3-Bis(5-Methoxy-3,4-Methylenedioxybenzyl)Butane-1,4-Diol Diacetate and 3-((1S)-1,5-Dimethyl-4-hexenyl)-6-methylene-1-cyclohexene, all share the common target of M-phase phosphoprotein 8. This suggests that benzocaine exerts its effects by modulating the activity of this protein, which in turn influences the expression of Histone H1.0. The presence of multiple benzocaine analogs with similar targets reinforces the idea that the interaction between benzocaine and Histone H1.0 is mediated through a shared molecular mechanism involving M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic link between benzocaine and Histone H1.0, highlighting the role of this protein in the cellular response to the drug.",
